Third-party components keep their own licences:

- Public Kaggle code of heliosli (R7 training code and the v4 view producer it builds on; Kaggle notebooks,
  Apache License 2.0): in training/sources/h6, data_prep/h6_v4/rsna/vendor/mainline, data_prep/h6_v4/rsna/reference
  and the H6 inference runtime.
- MONAI 0.6.0 (Apache License 2.0), vendored in data_prep/h6_v4/rsna/vendor/mainline/training/vendor_runtime/monai060
  and in the H6 inference runtime.
- timm (Apache License 2.0) and the other Python packages in requirements.txt and in the offline wheels: their own
  licences.
- Pretrained weights that are not redistributed here (README.md, Weights): CoAtNet-rmlp-2-384 from timm / Hugging Face,
  ConvNeXt-S 22k→1k from Meta, the SKM-TEA V-Net checkpoint published by heliosli on Kaggle.
- Public label tables of laymond and yunus (Kaggle datasets), used as two of the six report readers of Core6.
- External data: OAI (NIMH Data Archive) and fastMRI / fastMRI+ (NYU, Microsoft) are used under their own terms; no
  OAI or fastMRI images are included. No OAI-derived data are included either: the frozen H6 targets in
  training/sources/h6/assets hold the RSNA rows only, and the OAI targets (MOAKS grades and our VM reads of OAI
  knees), the OAI case roster and any NDA account details were removed (training/H6_RECIPE.md). The competition data
  are used under the competition rules and the RSNA MIRA licence.
